## 2.6 Architecture of the Platform

### 2.6.1 High-Level Architecture

Dash follows a three-tier architecture:

| Layer | Components & Responsibilities |
|-------|-------------------------------|
| Client Layer | Next.js app (UI rendering, routing). Manages auth sessions via Supabase SDK. |
| Application Layer | Next.js route handlers (API endpoints). Prisma client for database queries. |
| Data & Services Layer | Supabase Auth, PostgreSQL, Storage, Realtime |

### 2.6.2 UML Diagrams

**Use Case Diagram — Actors & Actions**

- **Student:** Register (with field/level, pending approval), login, view/create posts, view/edit profile, search users/groups, join events, send messages, use marketplace, report lost/found items
- **Student Admin:** View support tickets, approve/reject events, moderate flagged content, access admin console
- **Main Admin (School Admin):** Manage school settings, create fields/levels, approve/reject registrations, assign student admins, broadcast announcements

**Class Diagram — Core Domain Models**

| Model | Key Attributes |
|-------|----------------|
| User | id, student_id, school_id, field_of_study_id, level_id, role, is_student_admin, approval_status |
| School | id, name, domain, require_approval, admin_id |
| FieldOfStudy | id, name, description, school_id |
| Level | id, name, description, order, school_id |
| Community | id, name, type (FIELD_ONLY/LEVEL_ONLY/FIELD_AND_LEVEL/STUDENT_CREATED), school_id, field_of_study_id, level_id, is_auto_assigned |
| Post | id, author_id, content, images, audience, group_post_id, likes, comments |
| Event | id, title, date, location, organizer_id, approval_status, attendees |
| SupportTicket | id, user_id, title, description, category, priority, status |
| MarketplaceListing | id, seller_id, brand_id, title, price, category, condition, status |
| Brand | id, seller_id, name, description, logo |

**Sequence Diagram — Student Registration & Admin Approval Flow**

1. Student navigates to /register and selects university
2. System fetches available fields and levels for the selected school
3. Student enters Student ID, name, username, password, field of study, and level
4. System creates account in PENDING state
5. Student sees "Awaiting Approval" screen
6. Main Admin reviews pending registrations in Admin Portal
7. Admin clicks Approve
8. System updates approval_status to APPROVED and assigns student to 3 communities
9. Student signs in and completes onboarding
10. Student lands on Campus Feed

**Deployment Diagram**

```
Client Browser → Vercel CDN/Edge → Next.js (Vercel) → Supabase (Auth + PostgreSQL + Storage + Realtime)
```

