## 2.7 Security Strategy

### 2.7.1 Authentication & Access Control
- Secure account creation via Supabase Auth with hashed passwords
- Session tokens managed server-side
- Three roles: Student, Student Admin, Main Admin with scoped permissions
- Admin Portal (/admin-portal) requires separate Main Admin login
- Student Admin Console (/main/student-admin) restricted to isStudentAdmin users

### 2.7.2 Database Security — Row-Level Security (RLS)
- RLS enabled on all critical tables
- Each user can only access authorized rows
- Supabase service role key used exclusively in server-side routes

### 2.7.3 Data Protection & Privacy
- Only essential data collected: Student ID, name, field, level, password
- No email required — Student ID is primary identifier
- Admin Privacy Policy: admins cannot access private chats or personal messages
- All moderation actions logged for audit

### 2.7.4 Operational Security
- All credentials stored in environment variables
- Development and production environments kept separate
- Least privilege principle enforced

---

## 2.8 Performance & Scalability

### 2.8.1 Performance Considerations
- Next.js Image component for optimized images
- Code-splitting and lazy loading
- Pagination on all large lists (feed, search, marketplace)
- Database indexing on frequently queried fields

### 2.8.2 Scalability Considerations
- Multi-school architecture with school_id isolation
- Supabase scales horizontally within plan limits
- Vercel Edge Network for global content delivery

---

## 2.9 Testing Strategy

### 2.9.1 Levels of Testing
- **Unit tests:** Validation rules, utility functions
- **Integration tests:** API routes, Prisma queries
- **UI testing:** Key user flows (registration, approval, login, posting)

### 2.9.2 Manual Test Plan
1. Register a student with field/level selection → verify approval screen
2. Admin approves registration → verify community assignment
3. Student logs in → verify feed access
4. Create post → verify appears in feed
5. Create event → verify requires admin approval
6. List marketplace item → verify appears correctly
7. Submit support ticket → verify appears in My Tickets
8. Student admin accesses panel → verify ticket/event/flag management

---

## 2.10 Pages of the Application

### 2.10.1 Landing Page (Public)
The landing page introduces Dash with the headline "Your campus, all in one place" and displays platform statistics. Two CTAs: "Join Your Campus" and "Sign In".

### 2.10.2 Language Selection
Users can select English or French before registering. Language can be changed anytime in profile settings.

### 2.10.3 Student Registration — Join Dash
Students register by selecting their university, entering Student ID, name, username, password, and selecting their field of study and level from dynamic dropdowns populated by the database.

### 2.10.4 Awaiting Admin Approval
After registration, students see a confirmation screen explaining the approval process and next steps.

### 2.10.5 Admin Portal — Main Admin
The Admin Portal (/admin-portal) provides:
- Dashboard with metrics (students, pending approvals, flagged content, student admins)
- Pending tab: approve/reject registrations
- Students tab: manage enrolled students
- Flagged tab: review reported content
- School Settings tab: configure school details
- Fields management page (/admin-portal/fields): CRUD for fields of study
- Levels management page (/admin-portal/levels): CRUD for levels with reordering

### 2.10.6 Student Login — Sign In
Approved students log in with university selection, Student ID, and password.

### 2.10.7 Onboarding — First-Time Users
First-time users see a guided tour introducing the main features before landing on the feed.

### 2.10.8 Campus Feed — Home / Main Feed
The central hub showing posts from the school community, announcements, and group content. Tabs: Following, Trending, Peek. Channel filters available.

### 2.10.9 Campus Events
Events page with category filters and RSVP options. Events require admin approval before going live.

### 2.10.10 Campus Groups
Discover and join study groups, clubs, and organizations. Tabs: Discover, My Groups.

### 2.10.11 Campus Marketplace
Buy, sell, and trade items within the school community. Category filters and seller contact via messaging.

### 2.10.12 Lost & Found
Report and recover lost items. Tabs: Lost, Found, Resolved.

### 2.10.13 Search
Find people and groups within the campus. Tabs: People, Groups.

### 2.10.14 Messages — Direct Messaging
Private messaging between students. School-scoped for security.

### 2.10.15 Student Profile
Public profile showing posts, media, saved content, and settings. Editable fields: academic field, interests, bio.

### 2.10.16 Notifications
Aggregated activity feed with tabs: All, Announcements, Activity. Customizable notification preferences.

### 2.10.17 In-App Admin Console — Student Admin
Moderation dashboard at /main/student-admin showing:
- Support tickets to manage
- Pending events to approve/reject
- Flagged content to review
- Stats overview

### 2.10.18 Campus Broadcasting — Official Announcements
Admins can compose and broadcast announcements to all students or specific groups. AI assistant available for optimization.

### 2.10.19 Support Center
Students can submit support tickets in categories: Tech Support, Report Behavior, General Inquiry. Track ticket status in My Tickets.

---

## 2.11 Competitor Analysis

### 2.11.1 Direct / Functional Competitors
- **WhatsApp/Telegram:** Fast but unstructured, no verification or moderation
- **Discord:** Strong community features but no school-native identity
- **Facebook Groups:** Wide adoption but privacy concerns, no student ID verification

### 2.11.2 Institutional & Platform Competitors
- **School Portals/LMS:** Academic focus, not designed for social life
- **LinkedIn:** Professional networking, not for informal campus interactions

### 2.11.3 Competitive Advantages — Dash
| Advantage | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| Verified student identity | Student ID + admin approval ensures real enrolled students |
| Field/Level communities | Automatic grouping by academic program and year |
| Multi-school architecture | Each school has isolated, scoped environment |
| Integrated feature suite | Feed, events, marketplace, lost & found, messaging in one app |
| Admin control layer | Full oversight of registrations, content, and moderation |
| Student admin capabilities | Decentralized moderation by trusted students |
| AI-assisted tools | AI-powered announcement composition |

